16 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Two-panel scientific illustration explaining epigenetics. Panel A depicts DNA and nucleosomes, highlighting histone modification, DNA methylation, and chromatin remodelers with a legend. Panel B shows open versus closed chromatin, indicating the involvement of different chromatin marks and enzymes, with another legend identifying modification types.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating mRNA fate regulated by YTHDF1 and other protein interactions, showing pathways for translation, degradation, RNA storage during stress, and RNA stabilization, with specific protein complexes labeled in each stage.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the methylation-regulated signaling pathway involving genes and proteins such as GATA1, CLDN11, NFAT1, E-cadherin, Hopx, ITGA6, and their effects on CLDN11, E-cadherin, and epithelial\205mesenchymal transition \(EMT\), with inhibitory interactions indicated.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 60 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating upstream triggers such as radiotherapy stress, core phosphorylation hubs involving YAP, AKT, STAT3, and LATS1, and downstream signaling branches leading to EMT, immune evasion, cytoskeletal remodeling, motility, and treatment adaptation consequences in nasopharyngeal carcinoma \(NPC\).) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 61 0 R /Alt (Illustration comparing therapy-related side effects of radiotherapy and chemotherapy. Radiotherapy increases H3K27 acetylation in chromosomes, nucleosomes, and DNA, while chemotherapy reduces DNA methylation through DNMT3a, resulting in hypomethylation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 62 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 63 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing epigenetic therapy strategies for nasopharyngeal carcinoma linked to Epstein-Barr Virus, including targeting DNA methylation, histone modifications, and non-coding RNAs to activate tumor suppressor genes and silence oncogenic long non-coding RNAs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 64 0 R /Alt (Diagram depicting regulatory pathways involving MLN4924, PROTAC, and HDAC inhibitors, showing effects on NEDD8, VDAC2, RIM21, palmitoylation proteins, histone acetylation \(H3K27ac and H3K9ac\), mitochondrial membrane potential, membrane signaling, and oncogene transcription.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
